<%#
    The Android tutorial, as one scrollable page.

    Both phones show this once, on first run, as four swipeable cards. Web users
    never saw any of it, so the explanation of what the app is deliberately not
    for was reaching everyone except the people most likely to need it. The copy
    is the apps', word for word, so the three do not drift into explaining the
    idea differently — which is why the last card changed here at the same time
    as it changed on the phones.
%>
<%- include('partials/head') %>
            <div class="appbar__titles">
                <h1 class="appbar__title"><a href="<%= budget ? '/Budget/' + budget.UniqueId : '/' %>">How this works</a></h1>
                <% if (budget) { %><span class="appbar__sub"><%= budget.Name || "Weekly Budget" %></span><% } %>
            </div>
            <div class="appbar__actions">
                <a class="btn btn--text" href="<%= budget ? '/Budget/' + budget.UniqueId : '/' %>">Done</a>
            </div>
<%- include('partials/afterbar') %>
<article class="prose">
    <span class="prose__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11.8 10.9c-2.27-.59-3-1.2-3-2.15 0-1.09 1.01-1.85 2.7-1.85 1.78 0 2.44.85 2.5 2.1h2.21c-.07-1.72-1.12-3.3-3.21-3.81V3h-3v2.16c-1.94.42-3.5 1.68-3.5 3.61 0 2.31 1.91 3.46 4.7 4.13 2.5.6 3 1.48 3 2.41 0 .69-.49 1.79-2.7 1.79-2.06 0-2.87-.92-2.98-2.1h-2.2c.12 2.19 1.76 3.42 3.68 3.83V21h3v-2.15c1.95-.37 3.5-1.5 3.5-3.55 0-2.84-2.43-3.81-4.7-4.4z"/></svg></span>
    <h2>Budget your spending money</h2>
    <p>Start outside the app. Take what you earn, subtract the bills that never
       change — rent, insurance, subscriptions, loan payments — and whatever is
       left is your spending money.</p>
    <p>Split that across the weeks in the month, and you have your weekly target.</p>

    <span class="prose__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19.5 3.5 18 2l-1.5 1.5L15 2l-1.5 1.5L12 2l-1.5 1.5L9 2 7.5 3.5 6 2v14H3v3a3 3 0 0 0 3 3h12a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V2l-1.5 1.5zM16 20H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-1h11v2zm3-1a1 1 0 0 1-2 0v-3H8V5h11v14z"/><path d="M9 7h8v2H9zm0 3h8v2H9z"/></svg></span>
    <h2>Bills don't belong in here</h2>
    <p>There is deliberately nowhere to enter recurring income or expenses. Those
       amounts are already fixed, so leaving them out keeps the app focused on
       the one number that actually moves: what you spent this week.</p>
    <p>If money comes in mid-week — a refund, a gift, cash back — add it as an
       expense with a minus sign.</p>

    <span class="prose__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 11c1.66 0 2.99-1.34 2.99-3S17.66 5 16 5s-3 1.34-3 3 1.34 3 3 3zm-8 0c1.66 0 2.99-1.34 2.99-3S9.66 5 8 5 5 6.34 5 8s1.34 3 3 3zm0 2c-2.33 0-7 1.17-7 3.5V19h14v-2.5c0-2.33-4.67-3.5-7-3.5zm8 0c-.29 0-.62.02-.97.05 1.16.84 1.97 1.97 1.97 3.45V19h6v-2.5c0-2.33-4.67-3.5-7-3.5z"/></svg></span>
    <h2>Share it with your partner</h2>
    <p>One budget can live on as many devices as you like, and they all stay in step.</p>
    <p><% if (budget) { %>Open <a href="/Budget/<%= budget.UniqueId %>/Edit">Edit budget</a><% } else { %>Open Edit budget<% } %>
       and create an invitation, then send the link. Whoever opens it joins this
       budget, and you will both see the same running total.</p>
    <p>The link works once and expires after a week, so a forwarded one is
       harmless. The budget ID still works for older versions of the app, but it
       never expires — treat it like a password.</p>

    <span class="prose__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 1.01 7 1a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v18a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V3a2 2 0 0 0-2-1.99zM17 19H7V5h10v14z"/></svg></span>
    <h2>There is an app for both phones</h2>
    <p>This page works on the same budget as either app — same expenses, same
       total, in step within seconds.</p>
<%- include('partials/appLinks') %>
    <p>Or keep using this page: add it to the home screen and it behaves much
       like an app. <a href="<%= budget ? '/Budget/' + budget.UniqueId + '/Apps' : '/Apps' %>">Apps</a>
       has the details.</p>
</article>
<% if (budget) { %>
<%- include('partials/bottomnav', { budget: budget }) %>
<% } else { %>
<%- include('partials/beforenav') %>
<% } %>
<%- include('partials/scripts') %>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
